+# Native qualified budget plugin implementation plan
+
+> Use superpowers:executing-plans and test-driven-development in the isolated pinned worktree.
+
+**Goal:** Remove unsafe native-v2 GPU candidates through KAI's existing GPUOrderFn, preserving ordinary scheduling and physical device selection.
+
+**Architecture:** Root-pinned immutable measured budget projection, Gateway-owned immutable request records, and fresh Node-owned claim snapshots are distinct trust lanes. Existing informer caches provide raw objects before scoring. Each score rechecks only local versions, generation, deadlines and current Node epoch, then uses a session accounting view invalidated by Allocate/Deallocate callbacks. Retained active/retiring claims are never released by rollback or expiry.
+
+**Spec:** `native-qualified-budget.md`, with Root's approved request-producer split, local watch/cache freshness checks and injective unknown-group model.
+
+**Files:** new `pkg/scheduler/plugins/nativequalifiedbudget/{contract.go,provider.go,nativequalifiedbudget.go,accounting.go,*_test.go,testdata/*}`; plugin registration in `pkg/scheduler/plugins/factory.go`; schema/design documentation; generated changelog fragment.
+
+## Constraints and review focus
+
+- Default off; missing/malformed/stale inputs deny native-v2 candidates only. No network or JSON parsing inside GPUOrderFn.
+- Gateway/Source creates request records only after exact registered Pod/compiler/member/head/window custody. Node cannot invent requests or measured budgets.
+- Full-spec authorization stays in Gateway/Binder: KAI's compact cache does not preserve full executable fields.
+- Every actual advertised GPU on the candidate Node must be covered by the requested profile and current qualified epoch.
+- Known groups resolve only through a unique trusted-namespace reservation Pod and inventory mapping; never infer a UUID from a group/index.
+- Distinct unresolved groups consume distinct physical reservation slots; every possible destination must fit each group's aggregate demand. Do not sum unrelated groups on every device.
+- Retiring/absent-Pod claims remain charged; session rollback removes only provisional accounting. Binder retirement guard remains separate.
+
+## Task 1: closed contracts and real framework filtering
+
+- [x] Write failing tests using actual Session.FittingGPUs→GetNodePreferableGpuForSharing, raw informer objects and measured A/B fixture. Require native-full-A/safe-B routing and ordinary/default-off behavior.
+- [x] Implement closed Root budget, Gateway request and Node claim protocols; independent namespace/UID/reference and finite freshness checks. Test substitutions, malformed/duplicate JSON, complete inventory and current Node epoch.
+- [x] Implement production local informer provider and session invalidation. Test in-session updates, expiry and no API calls from scoring.
+- [x] Add measured MiB/count candidate filter and reservation-based UUID routing. Test retained retiring claims, dedup and foreign group/mapping denials.
+
+## Task 2: actual provisional allocation, rollback and verification
+
+- [x] Write real Statement Allocate/Pipeline/Rollback tests; duplicate scoring/events must not double-charge and rollback must restore capacity.
+- [x] Implement event-invalidated accounting from actual NodeInfo tasks plus immutable retained claim baseline. Test two unknown groups/distinct slots, accumulated same-group demand and known B availability.
+- [x] Register the plugin builder without changing default scheduler configuration; document producer/activation prerequisites and exact JSON schemas.
+- [x] Run focused/race/upstream touched-scope tests, build the targeted scheduler, and report the full-Go test boundary with real results.
+- [ ] Independent review before final source freeze; preserve original dirty checkout and do not install/push images or change any live workload.
+
+## Offline verification boundary
+
+Pinned Go 1.26.8: all 305 non-E2E packages completed with exit 0 (192 with
+tests, 113 without); envtest used local Kubernetes 1.35.0 with existing-cluster
+flags false and nonexistent kubeconfig. New Pipeline/Rollback regression was
+added after full-suite compilation and separately passed normally and under
+`-race`. Plugin/registration race tests, actual framework/gpu-sharing/gpupack
+tests, and linux/amd64 plus linux/arm64 scheduler builds passed. Draft2020-12
+schema and all three independently generated wire fixtures validate.
+
+`make validate` passed generation/manifests/clients/license/mocks/fmt/vet, then
+stopped at Docker image short-name resolution. Exact pinned local
+golangci-lint v2.11.3 with the same configuration separately passed (0 issues).
+Graft refresh failed writing its generated graph cache with ENOSPC; source
+hashes were unchanged. Full runtime integration, E2E/hardware tests and
+activation are not part of this offline qualification.
